    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "** Please register your interest **\n\nGeorge & Maguire Properties are delighted to present 16D Cherrywood Park, Loughlinstown, Dublin 18, an attractive two-bedroom detached bungalow occupying a particularly appealing position within this mature and established residential development.\n\nTucked away within a quiet cul-de-sac and positioned directly opposite a large open green, the property enjoys a wonderful sense of space and privacy. Detached bungalows are always sought after, and No. 16D offers an exciting opportunity for buyers seeking comfortable single-level living with the added potential to further enhance or extend the existing accommodation, subject of course to the necessary planning permission.\n\nInternally, the accommodation is well proportioned and comprises an entrance hallway with storage, a bright living room overlooking the front with an open fireplace, a fitted kitchen with direct access to the garden, two bedrooms with built-in wardrobes and a fully tiled bathroom.\n\nOne of the particularly attractive features of the property is the rear garden. Exceptionally private and not overlooked, it incorporates a generous patio area with steps leading to a charming sunken garden framed by mature planting, established flower beds and trees. It provides a wonderfully secluded outdoor space and further enhances the potential of this detached home.\n\nThe location is exceptionally convenient, with Loughlinstown providing easy access to the surrounding areas of Cabinteely, Shankill, Killiney and Cherrywood. The M50 and N11 are within easy reach, making the property particularly convenient for those commuting throughout Dublin, while a wide variety of shopping, recreational and everyday amenities are available nearby.\n\nWith its detached setting, quiet cul-de-sac position, outlook over a large open green, private rear garden and potential to extend, 16D Cherrywood represents an excellent opportunity to acquire a home with considerable potential in a highly convenient Dublin 18 location.\n\nAccommodation\n\nEntrance Hallway\nUPVC front door opens to the entrance hallway with a useful storage cupboard and access to the principal accommodation. Hot press with lagged cylinder.\n\nLiving Room\nA bright and comfortable living room overlooking the front of the property, featuring an open fireplace with marble surround, hearth and mantel. Fitted unit and recessed lighting.\n\nKitchen\nWell-appointed kitchen incorporating a comprehensive range of oak wall and floor-level units providing excellent storage. Fitted hob, oven and extractor hood, dishwasher and plumbing for washing machine. Tiled splashback, timber flooring and recessed lighting. A door provides direct access to the rear garden.\n\nBedroom One\nGenerous double bedroom with a wall of built-in wardrobes providing excellent storage.\n\nBedroom Two\nWell-proportioned bedroom with built-in wardrobes.\n\nBathroom\nFully tiled bathroom comprising a freestanding Triton shower, WC and wash-hand basin with vanity storage beneath. Wall-mounted mirrored storage cabinet, stainless-steel heated towel rail and recessed lighting.\n\n\nRear Garden\nA particularly private rear garden, which is not overlooked and enjoys a mature, secluded setting. A large patio area immediately adjoining the house provides an ideal space for outdoor dining and entertaining, with steps leading down to a sunken garden featuring attractive mature flower beds, established planting and trees. There is also side access to the property.\n\n\n"
